  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 9k-15 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \u2217 & 1 \\\\ \u2217 & -4 & \u2217 \\\\ 9k-15 & \u2217 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)-(9k-15)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6-(9k-15) \\\\  & =-9k+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9k+9 & =3{k}^{2}-45 \\\\ -3k+3 & ={k}^{2}-15 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k-18 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=3$ and $k=-6.$",
